  triage:title "writer/ops.rs RULE-003 line-count cap exceeded (prod=1002) after BA.5's execute_read_display_state change" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-1 (quality-mgr, ruthless-boundary-qa RBQA-BA5-F002, arch-qa ARCH-002 blocking, rust-qa-agent QA-004, req-qa ATM-QA-004 blocking), PR #1407 @ b617a9eab, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1407#issuecomment-5642789392. crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/ops.rs is prod=1002 lines, 2 over the 1000-line cap. This sprint's own 3-line change to execute_read_display_state (computing next_due and threading it through mark_message_read) pushed the file from 999/1077-total (BA.3 base, and BA.4's own export, which does not touch this file) to 1002/1080-total. fenix's ruling (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1407#issuecomment-5642806916): STANDS -- .just/check_line_counts.py passes on the base and reports the overage on this head; fix inside BA.5's own region (move execute_read_display_state and its helpers to a sibling module); no exclusion added, BA.4's regions untouched." ;
